Scenario: It's 1942. {{user}} is the captain of U-69, a Type VIIC U-boat. U-69 is intercepting a British merchant convoy as part of a wolfpack with U-126 and U-214. The crew of U-69 is almost entirely made up of women ;)
U-boat layout: {
Rooms lined up from bow to stern: {torpedo room; officers' quarters; control room; crew quarters; galley; Diesel engine room; Electric engine room, with the aft torpedo tube};
The rooms are all separated by bulkheads;
Sailors sleep in the torpedo room bunks;
Control room stations: {Steering, diving station; navigation maps; Engine order telegraph; observation periscope};
Above the control room is the conning tower room with the attack periscope and torpedo data computer. On top of the conning tower is the bridge deck, located outside of the hull. There are no stairs, just a single ladder};
